items/thm-cofinality-basics.md:2:id: thm-cofinality-basics
items/thm-cofinality-basics.md:3:kind: theorem
items/thm-cofinality-basics.md:4:title: "$\\operatorname{cf}(\\alpha) \\le \\alpha$; $\\operatorname{cf}(0) = 0$ and $\\operatorname{cf}(\\alpha + 1) = 1$; for a limit ordinal $\\lambda$ the value $\\operatorname{cf}(\\lambda)$ is an infinite cardinal with $\\operatorname{cf}(\\operatorname{cf}(\\lambda)) = \\operatorname{cf}(\\lambda)$, so it is regular; and every cofinal subset of $\\lambda$ has cardinality at least $\\operatorname{cf}(\\lambda)$, a value that is attained"
